    <statement><p>Calculate the integral:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle \int \frac{1}{(x+7)(x+9)}\,dx =</m>
<fillin characters="55" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.5\ln\mathopen{}\left(\left|x+7\right|\right)-0.5\ln\mathopen{}\left(\left|x+9\right|\right)+C</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><me>\frac{1}{(x+7)(x+9)}=\frac{A}{x+7}+\frac{B}{x+9},</me>
giving
<me>1 =  A(x+9)+B(x+7),</me>
or
<me>1 = (A+B)x+ (9 A+7 B).</me>
Solving for <m>A</m> and <m>B</m>, we find <m>A = 0.5</m> and <m>B = -0.5</m>,
so
<me>\int \frac{1}{(x+7)(x+9)}\,dx= \int\frac{0.5}{x+7}\,dx +
  \int \frac{-0.5}{x+9}\,dx = 0.5\ln\mathopen{}\left(\left|x+7\right|\right)-0.5\ln\mathopen{}\left(\left|x+9\right|\right)+C.</me>



</solution>
